# netsurf: grid items -- margins, borders, outer-height alignment, the container's height (patch 349)
# Generated 2026-10-30
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 348)
#
# A box's x/y is its padding edge everywhere in NetSurf (margin + border
# in from the containing block). Grid placement left out the item's top
# margin and its top and left borders. An item with margin-top sat on the
# row's top edge, though the row height already reserved the margin, and
# a bordered item pushed its border above and left of its cell. 347 added
# the left margin.
#
#  - layout_grid.c: y adds the item's top margin and top border; x adds
#    its left border.
#  - layout_grid.c: center/end alignment uses the item's outer height
#    (margins, borders, padding), not its content height.
#  - layout_grid.c: a definite container `height` stands. It was replaced
#    by the rows' total, so a `height: 60px` grid shrank to its content.
#    Under the default align-content (normal/stretch), the free height is
#    shared among auto rows; flex-start leaves it below them. A height
#    smaller than the rows also stands (they overflow).
#
# Gate: CSS-grid-item-offsets (GRIDOFS349 7/7, Chromium 7/7).
--- a/content/handlers/html/layout_grid.c
+++ b/content/handlers/html/layout_grid.c
@@ -1824,7 +1824,55 @@
